\
### Explicitly deferred\
\
Audio, save/load, menus/UI, particle effects, PBR materials, dynamic lighting, cross-face maze generation (guaranteed solvability), game rules/win conditions, multiple cube sizes in one session, runtime N resizing, final iOS touch controls.\
\
### Success criteria\
\
All five must be demonstrated on **both** a physical Mac and a physical iOS device, without code changes:\
\
1. Player navigates tile-to-tile through a 3\'d73\'d73 maze in first-person, passing through open passages and blocked by walls.\
2. Unknown tiles show animated fog. Stepping onto a tile triggers a fog dissolve revealing maze geometry. Revealed tiles stay revealed.\
3. Player triggers a slice rotation. It animates smoothly at 60 fps. The player's tile (if in the rotating slice) carries the camera. After animation, topology has changed and navigation works on the new layout.\
4. Crossing from one face to another transitions camera orientation smoothly with no facing-direction discontinuity.\
5. Frame time is consistently under 16.67 ms on both devices at 3\'d73\'d73.\
